  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-{x}^{2}-6x-8\\le 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-{x}^{2}-6x-8\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/bc265ca81928739c2154710d053e2ea19610861d6fdef65d49df497839a3c7d3.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge -2.$",
